2. Constraints ko kaise read karein?
    Symbol	    Meaning	                        Example
    ≤	        Less than or equal to	        1 ≤ n ≤ 100
    ≥	        Greater than or equal to	    n ≥ 1
    <	        Strictly less than	            i < n
    >	        Strictly greater than	        x > 0
    =	        Equal to	                    n = 10
    10⁵	        1 lakh	                        100000
    10⁶	        10 lakh	                        1000000
    10⁹	        100 crore	                    1000000000

Important: arr.size() aur arr[i] alag cheezein hain.
- arr.size() → array mein kitne elements hain.
- arr[i] → kisi particular index par element ki value.
- Java mein array ke liye arr.length use karte hain, arr.size() nahi. GFG statement mein arr.size() likha ho sakta hai kyunki woh generic terminology use kar raha hai.
  But, ArrayList me arr.size() ka use hota hai.

3. Constraints se kya pata chalta hai?
Constraints ke 3 main uses hain.
A. Input ki boundaries pata chalti hain.
Example: 1 ≤ n ≤ 10⁶

Tumhe pata hai ki array bahut bada ho sakta hai. Isliye unnecessarily nested loops use karne se bachna chahiye.

B. Algorithm ki time complexity choose kar sakte ho
    Maximum (n)	        Generally suitable approaches
    n ≤ 10	            Exponential approaches bhi possible ho sakti hain
    n ≤ 20	            Bitmasking / O(2^n) kuch problems mein
    n ≤ 10³	            O(n^2) aksar workable
    n ≤ 10⁵	            O(nlog n) ya O(n) prefer karo
    n ≤ 10⁶	            O(n) ya O(n log n) generally better

Ye sirf rough guidelines hain, guaranteed rules nahi. Actual suitability time limit, language, operations aur problem structure par depend karti hai.
C. Problem ka hidden hint mil sakta hai
Tumhare example mein:

1 ≤ arr[i] ≤ arr.size()+1

Agar array mein n elements hain aur values 1 se n+1 tak ho sakti hain, toh possible values ki total sankhya n+1 hai, lekin elements sirf n hain.

Isse hint milta hai ki question missing number ya missing value se related ho sakta hai. Lekin exact problem statement dekhe bina ise confirm nahi kar sakte.